@h1 Data model h1@

The value system that data-defs, records, collections, captures, and
@code load code@ all share: six value kinds, their JSON mapping, access paths,
conditions, and text coercion. Source: @code packages/parser/src/ast.ts code@.

@h2 The six DataValue kinds h2@

@table |rows [[Kind, Literal form, Standalone render], [stringValue, prose or a quoted string, escaped text], [numberValue, 42 or 3.14, the number as text], [booleanValue, true or false, true or false as text], [nullValue, null, empty in a table cell], [record, a brace map, a wit-record table], [collection, a bracket list, a wit-collection list]]| |caption DataValue kinds| table@

@@@pre
#title: Field notes          ~ stringValue
#count: 42                    ~ numberValue
#draft: true                  ~ booleanValue
#note: null                   ~ nullValue
#site: { name - Docs, year - 2026 }   ~ record
#tags: [ ref, spec, wit ]     ~ collection
pre@@@

Records carry an ordered @code fields code@ list of key/value pairs; collections
carry an ordered @code items code@ list. Data-def records need the
@strong hyphen strong@ delimiter; the colon form is call-site only.

@h2 Access paths h2@

A dotted lookup selects a field. Access is @strong fuzzy strong@: camelCase,
snake_case, and spaced keys all match.

@@@pre
#person: { firstName - Ada, role - Author }

Name is @person.first_name → Name is Ada
pre@@@

@aside(class note)
@strong Numeric index access renders unresolved. strong@ Verified:
@@@code @tags.0 code@@@ and @@@code @findings.0.claim code@@@ both emit
@@@code <span class="wit-unresolved"> code@@@ in the current build. Reach into a
collection with @@@code (each) code@@@ (below) or feed it to
@@@code @table |rows @ref| code@@@ instead. See
@a |href /docs/reference/limitations/| limitations a@.

aside@

@h2 Iteration h2@

@@@code (each @collection as item) … (end) code@@@ binds each element to
@code item code@. Inside the loop, reference it with @@@code @item code@@@ (a
bare reference), or @@@code @item.field code@@@ for a record field —
@strong not strong@ @@@code ::item:: code@@@ (that is capture interpolation, a
different mechanism).

@@@pre
#hands: [ { name - Marlow }, { name - Singleton } ]

@ul
(each @hands as item) @li @item.name li@ (end)
ul@
pre@@@

Iterating a non-collection raises @code E_NOT_ITERABLE code@.
@strong Fixture: strong@ @code 13-iteration/* code@.

@h2 Conditions h2@

The test in an @@@code (if …) code@@@ is either existence or a comparison.

@table |rows [[Form, True when], [if path, the path resolves to a value], [if path is X, the value equals X — identity], [if path equals X, the value equals X — comparison]]| |caption Condition forms| table@

@@@pre
(if @author) By @author.name (end)
(if @status is shipped) Live (else) Draft (end)
pre@@@

@strong Fixture: strong@ @code 12-conditionals/* code@.

@h2 JSON to Wit mapping h2@

The only shape that crosses the @code load code@ seam.

@table |rows [[JSON, Wit value], [object, record], [array, collection], [string, stringValue], [number, numberValue], [boolean, booleanValue], [null or undefined, nullValue]]| |caption JSON to Wit| table@

@h2 Text coercion h2@

When a value is placed in text (a table cell or inline), it is coerced:
number and boolean → their string form; @code nullValue code@ → an empty string.

@h2 typedValue h2@

A capture param carries a shape-probed @code typedValue code@ when it
@strong looks like strong@ a collection, record, or scalar literal; pure prose
keeps only its string value. This is what lets @@@code |rows @ref| code@@@ and
typed captures work — the table renderer reads @code typedValue code@.

